1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,210
Next, let's create a simple form for follow-up care.

2
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:05,880
We describe what we need:

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,530
a patient ID, goals, review notes, and the next review date.

4
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:17,040
VAAB presents the proposed tasks one at a time.

5
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:20,020
We check each task and confirm it in the chat.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,620
At this point, we can also ask for changes.

7
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:29,480
We then review the full plan.

8
00:00:30,050 --> 00:00:33,530
The build starts only after we give our final approval.

9
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:41,330
VAAB shows which tasks are complete and which are still running.

10
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:44,330
We have shortened the waiting time in this video.

11
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:48,250
Here is a generated form.

12
00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:52,270
We can see the fields we requested
and review the layout in the preview.

13
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:56,530
Now we ask for a small change.

14
00:00:57,380 --> 00:00:59,930
Rename the form to “Follow-up Care Plan”

15
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:02,130
and keep the other fields the same.

16
00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:07,360
The new title appears in the preview.

17
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:13,580
Next, we try the simulated release.

18
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:16,420
This does not publish the app online.

19
00:01:17,250 --> 00:01:20,050
A short survey lets users rate their experience

20
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:22,570
and share feedback on VAAB.

21
00:01:23,470 --> 00:01:25,340
We submit a sample response.

22
00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:29,440
This survey is separate from our research study.

23
00:01:33,730 --> 00:01:36,940
We can open the generated interface
in a separate preview tab

24
00:01:36,970 --> 00:01:38,340
to review its layout.

25
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:45,530
From a request to a reviewable interface.
